A palindrome program checks if the entered string or number is a palindrome. In this C++ program, I will demonstrate how to check if a given word or string is a palindrome.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <algorithm>

bool is_palindrome(const std::string& input) {
    std::string reversed_input = input;
    std::reverse(reversed_input.begin(), reversed_input.end());

    return input == reversed_input;
}

int main() {
    std::string input;

    std::cout << "Enter a word or string to check if it's a palindrome: ";
    std::cin >> input;

    if (is_palindrome(input)) {
        std::cout << input << " is a palindrome!" << std::endl;
    } else {
        std::cout << input << " is not a palindrome." << std::endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

To compile and run the program, you can use the following commands:
```
g++ palindrome.cpp -o palindrome
./palindrome
```

